  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd `delete_model {name}` to the MCP model tools.\nRun the existing `DeleteEntity` command as one undo step.\nRefuse unknown names, other entity kinds and fixtures.\nRefuse operation sources, feature selections, area picks and from-model stock dependencies by name.\nKeep refused changes out of history.\nDocument the tool in the MCP skill and record the decision.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe MCP tool table exposed import and placement but had no model deletion handler.\nAgents had to undo the import and every later change to remove a duplicate.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll six pins in `mcp_model_delete` failed on unchanged upstream/main c0c92ee86 and pass with the fix:\n\n- `delete_model_is_listed_and_round_trips_in_one_undo_step`\n- `delete_model_refuses_unknown_non_model_fixture_and_bad_arguments`\n- `delete_model_refuses_an_operation_source_without_history`\n- `delete_model_refuses_an_operation_selection_without_history`\n- `delete_model_refuses_an_area_pick_without_history`\n- `delete_model_refuses_a_setups_model_stock_without_history`\n\nRestoring `model_tools.rs` from upstream/main makes all six pins fail again.\nBypassing model validation, entity source, selection, area or stock checks makes the corresponding pin fail.\nRestoring the fix makes all six pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes all four steps.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\nThe build used an empty RUSTC_WRAPPER after the configured sccache stalled.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe diff for `*.nc` and `*.cl` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo GUI session, physical machine, batch gate or release gate ran.\nThe new MCP import fixture uses OBJ; STEP metadata restoration relies on the existing DeleteEntity command.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPRs #2253, #2149, #2134, #2092 and #2089 touch `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`.\nEach touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nNo open PR touches `model_tools.rs` or the new test and decision files.\nThis branch starts from upstream/main c0c92ee86.\n\nEffort: medium (no escalation)\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: Add undoable MCP model deletion with named refusals for models still used by operations, stock or fixture bindings.\nFixes #2444\n",
